        {
          "basis_risk": "Underlying evidence does not establish executable CFD economics.",
          "claim_id": "eia-storage-observed",
          "producer_layer": "OBSERVED_SOURCE_FACT",
          "text": "EIA release 2026-10-15: the weekly injection was 67 Bcf for the week ended 2026-10-09, versus the five-year same-week injection average of 90 Bcf. The stock level was 3567 Bcf, 45 Bcf above the five-year stock average and 143 Bcf below the prior-year stock level."
        },
        {
          "basis_risk": "Underlying evidence does not establish executable CFD economics.",
          "claim_id": "cc-gas-balance",
          "producer_layer": "CC_ANALYSIS",
          "text": "Capital Chronicle analysis: the smaller seasonal refill tightens the weekly balance at the margin, while the above-average stock cushion limits a simple shortage interpretation. It does not measure a market surprise or predict the CFD price."
        },
        {
          "basis_risk": "Underlying evidence does not establish executable CFD economics.",
          "claim_id": "cc-gas-short",
          "producer_layer": "CONDITIONAL_SCENARIO",
          "text": "The next weekly EIA release can test whether the small refill persisted; weather and a pre-release consensus are required to distinguish seasonality from a tradable surprise. If independent balance evidence confirms tightening, upward pressure is possible; warmer weather or supply recovery can reverse it. No price target or probability is estimated."
        },
        {
          "basis_risk": "Underlying evidence does not establish executable CFD economics.",
          "claim_id": "cc-gas-swing",
          "producer_layer": "CONDITIONAL_SCENARIO",
          "text": "Several weekly storage releases and weather-normalized balances must show the cushion narrowing; one small refill cannot establish a sustained deficit through the shoulder season. If independent balance evidence confirms tightening, upward pressure is possible; warmer weather or supply recovery can reverse it. No price target or probability is estimated."
        },
        {
          "basis_risk": "Underlying evidence does not establish executable CFD economics.",
          "claim_id": "cc-gas-long",
          "producer_layer": "CONDITIONAL_SCENARIO",
          "text": "Winter heating demand, supply response and export demand determine the inventory draw path; an October stock surplus can coexist with winter tightness, but the curve and CFD financing/roll are missing. If independent balance evidence confirms tightening, upward pressure is possible; warmer weather or supply recovery can reverse it. No price target or probability is estimated."
